Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.40.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.40.0 (archive 39): (1) regression fix - 0.39 required the leftward travel to exceed the vertical travel before revealing the picker, which made the user's swipes register as moves (archive 39 contains not a single '判定=呼出圆弧选择器'); now ANY leftward travel over 20pt reveals the picker; (2) a move now shows the float first when it had been hidden with the button (archive 39 moved it while hidden, so nothing visible happened); (3) new EXTREME-EDGE 20pt all-round zone (tag 990050 in the standalone window, 990052 in the status-bar mirror) that behaves exactly like the inner band but carries its own tag, so the logs answer the decisive question - does the outermost 20pt of the screen still receive touches while another app is full-screen? That decides between the edge route and process injection; (4) classification logs now include the raw dx/dy so thresholds can be tuned to the real feel. 0.39.0 (archive 38 conclusion applied): the log proved that ABOVE A FULL-SCREEN APP the float's CONTENT (a hosted FBScene layer) still receives touches while its surrounding grab bars (plain SpringBoard views) do not, and that the screen EDGE region still receives them (the status-bar mirror hot strip fired 3 times). Grabbing therefore moved to the edge: a right-edge PICKUP BAND where a one-finger vertical/diagonal drag MOVES the float window, a distinct leftward swipe reveals the arc picker and a TWO-finger vertical drag resizes the float proportionally around its centre; the arc picker is pinned at the vertical middle of the screen once revealed, only the highlight follows the finger.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
